{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767792-solar-with-above-average-skill","id":767792,"title":"Solar with above average skill","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-17T06:47:40-08:00","id":767792,"title":"Solar with above average skill","content":"In EX3 has someone ever tried to do a character that instead of focusing on one skill goes for a more broader spread of skill points?<br /> For example, instead of Melee 5 and 6 charms Melee 3 and Brawl 3 with 3 charm each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T06:56:41-08:00","id":767795,"title":"","content":"It's certainly much more feasible in 3e than it was in 2e. Where it really bites you is Charm stat mins. A lot of Charms are Ability 4-5 even at E1-E2. So this isn't a bad idea in tertiary focus areas but with your Supernal, you'll be getting relatively little out of that til you raise the Ability.<br /> <br /> You're not going to be behind so much as you may not be able to buy what you want to buy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 11-17-2015, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T07:10:07-08:00","id":767805,"title":"","content":"I decided to try this out for my first character in 3e. My highest skill is at 4 (War, also my supernal) and everything else is 3 or lower. It's been going well enough so far, but it's still early days for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:21:22-08:00","id":767863,"title":"","content":"It is something that works fairly well if the entire group does it, otherwise it just leaves you behind, especially the way bonus points work but also in general as specialists usually overshadows you at every point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:40:02-08:00","id":767882,"title":"","content":"I did Abilities at most 2 as an exercise to see what was the minimum XP total a character could have at the end of character creation. You have to spread your charms a lot to be able to pick 15 in that case. But it was doable, so at 3 you still have some leeway and more charms to pick than what I did.<br /> <br /> Maybe it works better in a small group of players where a generalist can shine. But if you have a full circle maybe you'll suffer from a &quot;anything you can do someone can do better&quot; situation for a bit there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:49:42-08:00","id":767894,"title":"","content":"I agree with the statements about Charm minimums, I do wish that had gotten a little more reasonable spread, at least up through Essence 2. That said, I believe someone with a wider spread in ability dots will be more versatile than even a group of specialists. Ex3 puts heavier value on a lot of stats even in combat.<br /> <br /> You could be an Archery guy, but you're not that great in close range, so take some brawl or melee.<br /> Awareness will get you a decent Join Battle AND help you spot that guy sneaking up on you.<br /> Stealth will help you sneak up on the guys!<br /> Resistance lets you get some OX body and fight off poisons, but you also took some dodge to help with your disengages.<br /> But while you're at it, don't forget your Athletics so you can rush them too!<br /> All the while, you're flexing some occult muscle for when spirits come up (Occult is also a good ability for charms with less than 5 early on. More options than some others).<br /> <br /> Having 3's in all of those actually makes you very versatile in 3rd Edition, compared to the guy who has 5 in Melee and Resistance and Dodge and 1 or 2 in the rest. You will cover more situations decently and have room for improvement, which is something I value a lot in my game. Sometimes I play my character concept out early on in a long campaign if I max everything out in the beginning. Nothing to advance to without breaking my concept and making my bare-knuckle brawler suddenly a sorcerer for no reason because too-much XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 11-17-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:57:50-08:00","id":767901,"title":"","content":"I should clarify that I don't necessarily advocate all character concepts that go for a wide spread of medium-high ability in stats. I'm a big believer in justify your character stats and not every characters makes sense to have a big spread of abilities as high as 3. But it does make sense that many characters will have at least 1 if not 2 in most of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:13:13-08:00","id":767915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767792-solar-with-above-average-skill?p=767894#post767894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cut for space</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that was what i was thinking. <br /> I had this idea of a charming warrior with a strange fighting style where he doesnt own a weapon, he disarms his opponent and use his weapon against him. So i needed brawl, melee, dodge and presence as main abilities. But then i also need awareness for join battle, resistance for ox body, athletics for mobility(they guy is a little acrobatic), integrity so i dont get duped by everyone i meet and maybe occult if i need to kill a god.<br /> When i spread the skill points there is no place for a 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:36:59-08:00","id":769189,"title":"","content":"Instead of making a new thread i use this.<br /> Did anyone also make a character where the skills and attributes where mismatched, like a combat character with social primary?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:50:45-08:00","id":769197,"title":"","content":"What do you consider a combat character? Personally I try to make all characters have some combat investment...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:19:41-08:00","id":769217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767792-solar-with-above-average-skill?p=769197#post769197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you consider a combat character? Personally I try to make all characters have some combat investment...</div> </div> </div> </div>A combat character is (fairly obviously) a character whose primary sphere of expertise, and interest, is combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did anyone also make a character where the skills and attributes where mismatched, like a combat character with social primary? </div> </div> </div>With things like Nightingale style, being primary social isn't such a terrible thing! The form lets you add your Performance to the raw damage of your withering attacks, for example. It's something I really want to try soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:57:08-08:00","id":769244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767792-solar-with-above-average-skill?p=769217#post769217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A combat character is (fairly obviously) a character whose primary sphere of expertise, and interest, is combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but i was thinking something like a character with a lot of skill point in combat abilities like brawl and dodge but in attributes he is focused in social.<br /> So brawl 5 presence 3 dex 3 charisma 5. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:09:36-08:00","id":769260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767792-solar-with-above-average-skill?p=769244#post769244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but i was thinking something like a character with a lot of skill point in combat abilities like brawl and dodge but in attributes he is focused in social.<br /> So brawl 5 presence 3 dex 3 charisma 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I mean, you still use Dex to hit, but you can raise that enough to be competent, and having Performance can make up for your lack of Strength, since it adds damage (at least with Silver Nightingale). If you pick stuff that doesn't scale with social stats AT ALL then you're going to be worse off, but depending on the game I'm sure you could still manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:25:52-08:00","id":769882,"title":"","content":"Forgetting about combat, its a character that has his skill and attributes are miss matched. Medicine 5, Int 3, Str 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:43:20-08:00","id":769892,"title":"","content":"I guess I have no idea what you're asking, since all of your posts say different things to me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:15:00-08:00","id":769915,"title":"","content":"When someone want to make a warrior he picks combat abilities and physical primary, if he wants a social character he picks social abilities and social attributes primary.<br /> Im asking if anyone tried a warrior with combat abilities and social attributes primary or social character with social abilities and physical primary or any other combination that involves the mental abilities and attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:34:19-08:00","id":769928,"title":"","content":"I often do combat characters with Mental primary (Usually heavy Int, not even Wits for JB). I like philosopher warrior trope a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}